config BR2_PACKAGE_SPLASH
	bool "splash"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBDRM if BR2_PLASTRON_DEVICE != "brick" && BR2_PLASTRON_DEVICE != "smartpro"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_ZLIB if BR2_PLASTRON_DEVICE = "brick" || BR2_PLASTRON_DEVICE = "smartpro"
	help
	  ZyperOS's boot animation, from the moment the panel lights until
	  ZyperOS takes the display over - which it does as soon as it is
	  ready, never waiting for the animation. The kernel leaves the
	  panel dark (see board/px2/boot.cmd), so this is also the first
	  thing to light it.

	  On the TrimUI Brick (BR2_PLASTRON_DEVICE "brick") it is splash-fb, which draws
	  on the framebuffer instead, from the moment it exists.
